  biomeName: Labyrinth Trenches
  minDepthMeters: 1500
  maxDepthMeters: 2000
  shortDescription: Intersecting deep V-shaped canyons forming a predator maze.
  isPlaceholder: 0
  visitPurpose: Transition biome. Come here to push deeper, find better materials,
    and follow strong natural shapes and search obvious pockets.
  commonRewardHook: Reliable value comes from Copper Ore and Cobalt Alloy.
  rareRewardHook: 'The rare pull is real: Iron Composite and Copper Wire.'
  landmarkIdentity: Labyrinth Trenches reads through spires, steps, and big natural
    crowns. Landmarks should feel large and route-defining.
  safePocketIdentity: Safe pockets exist, but they must be earned by reading the
    terrain.
  riskSummary: 'Main failure mode: bad drops and exposed lines, then overstaying
    for loot. Creature pressure stays medium.'
  extractionFocus: 'Targeted node work along long rock lines and exposed shelves.
    Mid-depth: favor stone pockets and hard-form nodes, then return before greed
    stretches the route.'
  landmarkGuidance: Dominant landmark is main ridge line. This slot should read through
    parallel ridge family and stepped breaks; use vertical forms to keep heading.
